  "id": "theslip",
  "note": "THE SLIP: the fence nobody signposts, in the old weigh-house at the top of the lay-by off The Gate Road, beside the Shingles (docs/proposals/marrow-midrises.md). A weigh slip is the ticket a weighbridge clerk hands a lorry driver; the name was there before Sluice was.\n\nA squat brick office stands forward of a lower store behind it. The office front carries the steel door with its lamp and spyhole light, the clerk's hatch plated over with a steel shutter, and the old window bricked to a slot of wire glass. The weighbridge kit is still bolted on: conduit to where the plates were, a slack cable to a lamp post that still works, yellow-banded kerb bollards. The store has aerials and a dish; there are bins and a yard shutter at the back.\n\n⚠ NO LETTERING ANYWHERE. A blank front is the one thing that tells you what it is.\n\nIt stands in for the `slipback` arm (`replaces`), which stays in LEGACY_MODELS.",
  "pal": "ty_oc_brick",
  "replaces": "slipback",
